{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q223099","formula":"C₂₁H₁₆","hill":"C21H16","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":16.0},"names":{"en":"Methylcholanthrene","ru":"Метилхолантрен"},"descriptions":{"en":"Methylcholanthrene is a highly carcinogenic polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon produced by burning organic compounds at very high temperatures. Methylcholanthrene is also known as 3-methylcholanthrene, 20-methylcholanthrene or the IUPAC name 3-methyl-1,2-dyhydrobenzo[j]aceanthrylene. The short notation often used is 3-MC or MCA. This compound forms pale yellow solid crystals when crystallized from benzene and ether.","ru":"Метилхолантре́н (сокр. МХА) — органическое соединение, известный полициклический ароматический углеводород, образующийся из продуктов сгорания топлива, нефтепродуктов, бытового мусора, в результате риформинга бензантрацена, происходящего при больших температурах. Входит в состав смога, сигаретного дыма."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":1674,"mass":268.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=C2CCC3=C2C(=CC4=C3C=CC5=CC=CC=C54)C=C1","inchikey":"PPQNQXQZIWHJRB-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-methyl-1,2-dihydrobenzo[j]aceanthrylene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1674","atoms":37,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.006,"y":1.168,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.813,"y":0.061,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.841,"y":2.424,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.137,"y":0.416,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.303,"y":1.904,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.385,"y":1.015,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.35,"y":-1.248,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.951,"y":-0.299,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.106,"y":-0.573,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.049,"y":-1.411,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.384,"y":-0.439,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.332,"y":-2.258,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.224,"y":2.135,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.697,"y":-1.916,"z":-0.001,